      "text": [
        "5523 - وَ قَدْ رُوِيَ عَنِ اَلصَّادِقِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ : أَنَّهُ سُئِلَ عَنْ قَوْلِ اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ ۝ فَإِنْ آنَسْتُمْ مِنْهُمْ رُشْداً فَادْفَعُوا إِلَيْهِمْ أَمْوٰالَهُمْ ۝\nقَالَ \"إِينَاسُ اَلرُّشْدِ حِفْظُ اَلْمَالِ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5523 - It was narrated from Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as), that he was asked about the saying of Allah (swt), the Exalted and Glorious:\n\"But if you perceive in them sound judgment, then deliver their wealth to them\"\n(Surah An-Nisa 4:6).\nImam (as) said: \"Perceiving sound judgment means the ability to safeguard wealth.\""
        ]
      }
